WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.389 --> 00:00:17.460
Good morning John; it's Monday, January 15th,
and I'm sitting in front of the new Brotherhood

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:23.770
2.0 website which you can find at Brotherhood2.com.
I'd appreciate any suggestions or comments.

00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:27.289
The podcast isn't quite working, but we'll
get there.

00:00:27.289 --> 00:00:32.460
Well, I'm feeling better. I'm not feeling
great. But now I've got this voice, it's like

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:40.101
not so much of a voice, it's just little popping
noises. Aaaaaahh. One of the advantages is

00:00:40.101 --> 00:00:45.300
that I'm kind of a baritone now. I guess I'm
usually a baritone, but maybe I'm a bass?

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.219
Maybe I'm a bass now.

00:00:47.219 --> 00:00:55.250
(sings) Do not forsake me though you know
I must spend...

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:58.859
So I went to Barnes and Noble yesterday. I
had to walk up to the lady at the desk because

00:00:58.859 --> 00:01:04.589
I didn't know where they would keep this book,
and I had to say, "I'm looking for a book,

00:01:04.589 --> 00:01:12.450
it's called 'We Wish to Inform You That Tomorrow
We Will Be Killed With Our Families'," and

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:17.990
she said "That's catchy!" So I brought the
book home, and then something interesting

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:18.990
happened.

00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:50.750
So yeah, it didn't happen. Um, I'm not saying
that the Brotherhood 2.0 book club is not

00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:56.270
a good idea, I'm just saying that right now
I'm going to have to avoid your genocide book

00:01:56.270 --> 00:02:00.789
for a little while. And when I say a little
while, I mean, like, less than a week. So

00:02:00.789 --> 00:02:04.020
I'll probably start it for Brotherhood 2.0
Friday.

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:10.440
Brotherhood 2.0 Agreement Moment! That's right,
John and I agreed on something! I think it's

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:14.580
a great idea for us to do our happy dances
for three minutes and thirty seconds. That

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:19.920
sounds like a perfect Brotherhood 2.0 project
idea! I don't have Daniel Biss, but I do have

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:25.280
this. It's what the University of Montana
gave me for all of my hard work. 3.5 minutes

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:33.140
times 60 seconds in a minute divided by 5
seconds per clip is 42.

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:37.750
Now there are several amazing things about
this idea:

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:41.290
First, is that you got the math really, very
wrong.

00:02:41.290 --> 00:02:46.000
Second remarkable thing about this idea is
that Daniel Biss commented within like, three

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:50.810
seconds of you posting the video and told
you that you were wrong. It must be very convenient

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:54.730
to have your own personal mathematician. I
gotta get me one of those!

00:02:54.730 --> 00:03:01.020
Last, and most remarkable about this idea
is that we now know the question.

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:04.470
What are you talking about?

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:10.262
Oh, sorry! Well, the answer to life, the universe,
and everything is 42, right? So the question

00:03:10.262 --> 00:03:14.640
must be, "How many happy dance clips does
it take to fill up a Brotherhood 2.0 segment?"

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:17.670
We really are doing some amazing things here.

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:22.019
I've been very impressed by the number and
quality of Misprinted Business Card Utilization

00:03:22.019 --> 00:03:28.330
ideas. Thank you very much; I will be discussing
those and other sundrys on Wednesday.

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:30.209
John, I'll see you tomorrow.

